Generated code under src/cim100/model/ and the IR snapshot under codegen/snapshot/ are
derived from the IEC CIM UML model (CIM100: iec61970cim17v40_iec61968cim13v13b_iec62325cim03v17b,
published by the UCA International Users Group, CIM Users Group). The UML project file states:
"The entire work provided in the UML project file is dedicated to the public domain. As such,
it is Open Source document using an Apache 2.0 License." The model file itself is not
redistributed here; tools/fetch_model.py downloads it from its pinned public source.

examples/mvlv-networks reads data from Team-Nando/MV-LV-Networks
(https://github.com/Team-Nando/MV-LV-Networks, BSD-3-Clause). That data is not redistributed
here.

src/cim100/profiles/data/cgmes_3_0.json is derived from the CGMES 3.0 vocabularies (RDFS2020) of
entsoe/CGMES-AP (https://github.com/entsoe/CGMES-AP, Apache-2.0, commit
e96dd4e323b1e2236e141dd03bf9adea81672e00; IEC 61970-600-2:2021 profiles). The European extension
classes of the generated model come from the EA model of cimug-org/CGMES-CIM17
(https://github.com/cimug-org/CGMES-CIM17, Apache-2.0, commit
1c7708f5d3bde53e154201707f31961573868cf2). Neither is redistributed here; tools/fetch_profiles.py
downloads them from their pinned public sources.

No ENTSO-E test data is redistributed. The opt-in test of the ENTSO-E CGMES 3.0 Conformity
Assessment Test Configuration (MicroGrid BaseCase v3.0.2, owned by ENTSO-E) downloads the files from
a pinned public copy and checks their sha256 at test time.

